.TH DIFF 1 "October 4, 2026" "MachO-explorer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diff \- structural differences between two Mach-O binaries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diff
.I binary-a
.I binary-b
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-arch= name ]
.RB [ \-\-max= n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports what changed between two binaries, over structural facts only: which
architectures are present, which header flags are set, which load commands and
sections exist, and which symbols are defined.
.SH WHY NOT CMP
.B cmp
between two builds of one source reports that every byte from the load base onwards
differs, because PIE and ASLR move every address, a dependency bump moves a dylib's
version fields, and a rebuild moves any timestamp. "Everything changed" cannot
distinguish a rebuilt binary from a different program, and cannot tell a reviewer
that the one thing they cared about did not move.
.PP
None of the facts compared here move on a rebuild, and all of them change when the
program does.
.SH THREE LISTS
.TP
.B differences
structural changes. The verdict is computed from these alone.
.TP
.B buildMetadata
UUIDs, and the presence of signing and provenance commands.
.TP
.B sizeChanges
section sizes, reported because they matter and counted separately.
.PP
Build metadata is reported rather than hidden, and kept out of the verdict. A tool
that called every rebuilt pair "changed" would be
.B cmp
with better manners; one that hid the UUID would be refusing an answer the caller
asked for.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
no structural differences
.TP
.B 1
there are structural differences \- a negative answer, not a failure
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.TP
.B 3
a file could not be read
.PP
Two builds of one program exit 0 with
.B buildMetadata
full. That is the case this tool exists for, and failing it would be absurd.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-arch= name
compare only this architecture
.TP
.BI \-\-max= n
cap on symbol names listed per direction (default 20). Counts are always exact; a
19,000-symbol binary would otherwise produce a diff nobody reads past the first line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
diff v1.0/libthing.dylib v1.1/libthing.dylib
diff \-\-json a b | jq '.data.differences[].category' | sort | uniq -c
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fingerprint (1),
.BR audit (1),
.BR describe (1)